      "message": "This logic appears to be almost identical to the tcpci_tcpm_get_cc() routine.\n\nThe one change is this function always checks CC1 state when DRP is off, while tcpci_tcpm_get_cc() checks both CC1 and CC2 state.\n\nAccording the comment at line 151, the CC1/CC2 states are the same when DRP is off, so I would expect both tcpci_tcpm_get_cc() and this function to generate the same cc1 and cc2 return values.\n\nAre the issues resolved if this routine is changed to:\n\n    static int rt1715_get_cc()\n    {\n        rv \u003d tcpci_tcpm_get_cc(port, cc1, cc2);\n        if (rv)\n            return rv;\n        rv \u003d rt1715_init_cc_params(port, rt1715_polarity[port] ? *cc2 : *cc1);\n    }",
